From 8ff4797957e96de3ce5c493cdcda1bd4cee41212 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: colum <git@volf.co>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:18:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] dsv41: TF_DS_PDL (off by default) programmatic dependent
 launches for the hand-written kernels, and the nsys gap script the pair run
 will use to size it

Switch: TF_DS_PDL ("1" or "on"; unset, "0", "off" or anything else: off). Read at load on every rank (ops.zig's Ops.load, next to the spec read; exact.zig's Exact.load) through ops.zig's onValue/pdl_env (onValue made pub for exact.zig's use; no other behavior change), stored as o.pdl / x.pdl. Both ranks read it; no fingerprint bit, no switches bit: it changes no frames and no bytes (launch timing only, and the pair may run mixed ranks bit-identically - setting it alike on both is the convention, like the other serve switches). native.zig's purpose comment carries the one line for it (not to be confused with TF_RDMA_PDL / TF_DS_TRITON_PDL; changes no frames, no bytes; no fingerprint bit, no switches bit).

The contract (CUDA programming guide; Baseten's crates/kernels/cu/common.cuh:14-15; this repo's dsv41/rdma_gather.cu pdl_enter):
- Every kernel in the four files takes int pdl as its LAST parameter and, at its entry, before any global read, exactly like rdma_gather's pdl_enter (one such inline per file, copied per file; no cross-file includes):
    #if defined(__CUDA_ARCH__) && __CUDA_ARCH__ >= 900
        if (pdl) { asm volatile("griddepcontrol.wait;" ::: "memory"); asm volatile("griddepcontrol.launch_dependents;" ::: "memory"); }
    #endif
  Every thread block executes both when pdl != 0. If the predecessor never executes launch_dependents (or is a plain kernel), the trigger happens implicitly when all of the predecessor's blocks exit - a PDL'd dependent's wait then blocks until the predecessor completes and flushes to global memory, which is fully correct either way.
- Every launch of these kernels passes cudaLaunchAttributeProgrammaticStreamSerialization = 1 (cuda.launch's .pdl, which selects cuLaunchKernelEx; plain cuLaunchKernel otherwise): ops.zig's go() helper and every direct launch site, and exact.zig's five launch sites. The host-side development launchers in torch_ops pass pdl = 0 (their C entry-point ABI is unchanged), as do the raw C launchers; nemotron's and vit.zig's launches pass trailing 0 (below). With the switch off, every launch takes .pdl = false and every kernel takes pdl == 0, so the asm is never even branched to: the instruction stream is today's.
- A PDL'd kernel after a non-PDL predecessor is safe (implicit completion). Stream capture is supported: the captured attribute records as a programmatic edge (cudaGraphDependencyTypeProgrammatic); nothing to do. Bits are identical: same launches, same inputs, same arithmetic.

Kernel files (int pdl last, pdl_enter at entry):
- zig/kernels/cuda/dsv41_ops.cu: 27 of its 28 kernels (including tf_ds_accept_chain_kernel from 0124). The one exception, tf_ds_l2_prefetch_kernel, is EXCLUDED: it reads the NEXT kernels' weights into L2 and must not run mid-flight against its predecessor's working set, so it neither takes pdl nor launches with the attribute; it stays a full stop like today (ops.zig does not pass .pdl for it either).
- zig/kernels/cuda/dsv41_torch.cu: all 5 (tf_ds_rms_norm_kernel, tf_ds_compress2_kernel, tf_ds_rope_kernel, tf_ds_bf16_scale_kernel, tf_ds_hc_mean4_kernel).
- zig/kernels/cuda/torch_ops/pointwise.cu: all 3 (tf_bf16_to_f32_kernel, tf_f32_to_bf16_kernel, tf_tap_add_kernel).
- zig/kernels/cuda/torch_ops/movement.cu: all 3 (tf_copy_spans_kernel, tf_gather_rows_kernel, tf_strided_copy_kernel).

Excluded, and why:
- tf_ds_l2_prefetch_kernel (above).
- dsv41_shard.cu (TF_DS_KV_SHARD's e.shard.*: the fetch/select/union kernels launched from shard_ops.zig): out of this patch; the known next candidate for the same treatment. (Its ring stage/collect pair already carries the attribute via rdma.zig's TF_RDMA_PDL.)
- The torch_ops files not among the four above (grammar_mask, nucleus, logprob, topk/argmax/indexing/cast_f64/norm_rotary, nemotron_*): none are launched by the served decode path or the e.ops/e.exact wrappers; skipped and noted here for the record.
- Two launch sites outside ops.zig/exact.zig had to change for the ABI alone (the trailing kernel parameter changed under them): vit.zig's eight direct vision-tower launches of these kernels (k_rope, k_rot, k_to_bf16, k_add, k_silu_mul, k_unfold, k_gelu, k_span) and nemotron's cuda_torch_ops.zig launches of tf_bf16_to_f32 (pointwise image) and tf_strided_copy (movement image). They pass trailing 0 and take no PDL attribute; TF_DS_PDL is read at load in ops.zig/exact.zig only, so the switch does not reach the vision tower or Nemotron. vit.zig's rmsNorm calls ride exact.zig, which does carry the attribute when the switch is on.
- tools/dsv41-zig/rec/zrec_torchlab.py raw-launches these fatbins over ctypes: its argument lists gained the trailing c_int(0) so the qualification harness still launches against the new ABI (bits identical).

Bits: identical. Launch timing only. Gates on the pair (not run on this host; host-only patch): tools/exact.py IDENTICAL with TF_DS_PDL=1; then the nsys script below (or tf-dsv41-lanes --profile / TF_DS_ROUND_PROFILE) to size the overlap the chain buys on GB10. The kit's Triton kernels already launch PDL (TF_DS_TRITON_PDL is on in the served build; zig/src/families/dsv41/tri.zig) - this closes the chain for the hand-written kernels between them.

The nsys script: tools/nsys_breakdown.py (new, untracked on purpose - no commits in the Sparks repo from here). Modelled on Baseten's tools/nsys_breakdown.py, same CLI shape and output format: reads the sqlite of `nsys export --type sqlite -o out.sqlite out.nsys-rep`; groups this engine's kernel names (scatter/gather/byte movers; top-k / selection; norm/rope/cast/compress (exact); head/sampler/drafter (our kernels); clock (marks); L2 prefetch; RDMA gathers; NCCL / all-reduce; kit Triton kernels (tri_ prefix - the recorded names are unknown until a trace exists; the --help epilog tells the operator to adjust the prefix if the trace shows otherwise); embed; other); steps segmented by a chosen kernel (--first, default tf_ds_clock_kernel: the start-of-round clock kernel opens a round when TF_DS_ROUND_PROFILE=1/2 (or --profile plus TF_DS_CLOCK_MARKS) is active; with TF_DS_GRAPHS=1 each stretch of the round gets one, so the script segments stretches - pass your own --first); mean wall time per step; a markdown table of launches/step, us/step, share. Does NOT filter `graphNodeId is not null` by default (this engine runs eager rounds when GRAPHS=0; Baseten's filter hides everything there); --graphs-only applies it. --device/--kernels/--top kept as in the model; the (no kernel running) guard kept; sane exit codes; the --help epilog documents producing the export, that whether nsys works on GB10/sm_121 is UNCHECKED, and that the script only reads the sqlite. Self-test run here: a synthetic 221-row fixture (5 tf_ds_clock_kernel boundaries, 4 steps) printed the table; python3 -m py_compile clean. NOT verified against a real pair trace.

Tests (host): zig build test green (this host's flaky runner reported one phantom "failed command" on an earlier run - the dsv41 family binary passes standalone 409/409 - its "failure" is sched_setaffinity errno 22 in this sandbox, unrelated to this patch - and the full re-run passed clean). No launch-Config-enumerating test pattern existed in ops.zig (the launch-geometry test covers blocks() only; the switches parse-test pattern is the spec-sample one), so no new launch-enumeration infrastructure was built; one parse test for TF_DS_PDL was added next to the spec-sample parse test. The .cu byte-correctness is pair-gated (exact.py); say so. Type-check/build: zig build install native -Dfatbins=... succeeds (binaries rebuilt).

Judgement calls:
- vit.zig, nemotron's cuda_torch_ops.zig and zrec_torchlab.py were not in the task's file list; they were mandatory ABI repairs (the trailing kernel parameter changed under them), made with trailing 0 / no attribute, matching the development-launcher rule. The switch does not reach them.
- The four .cu files were checked only with a clang stub syntax check: scratch stub CUDA headers, plain `clang++ -fsyntax-only -x c++` on copies with the <<<>>> launch tokens stripped (plain clang has no CUDA frontend), once with the host preprocessor path and once with -D__CUDA_ARCH__=900 (exercising the pdl_enter asm path). Honest limits: this checks syntax and the plain-call type agreement of the host launchers' argument lists against the new kernel signatures; it does NOT check nvcc name mangling, ptxas, or the sm_90 asm encoding. The image nvcc is the first real compile of these files; nothing here has been run on a GPU.
- native.zig carries only the one purpose-comment line; no fingerprint bit, no switches bit, no env read there.
- l2_prefetch deliberately does not take the parameter (above).
- ops.zig's onValue was made pub (exact.zig reuses it and pdl_env); no other behavior change.

Unverified on the pair: exact.py IDENTICAL with TF_DS_PDL=1 (the point of the gate); the size of the overlap (nsys on GB10/sm_121 is UNCHECKED; the script has not seen a real trace); graph capture of the PDL edge (constructed from the CUDA graph model, not observed); the vision tower under TF_DS_PDL=1 (rmsNorm rides exact.zig's attribute; the eight other vision kernels take pdl = 0 by design).

Patches: this is 0126 in the decode-step-structure series; item C of docs/baseten-ultrafast-plan.md.

